{"id": "EUVD-2026-86665", "enisaUuid": "4ccf07c6-2df0-3dbc-be72-9470d1bf0df5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/sched: sfq: clamp quantum in change path\n\nsfq_change() accepts any non-negative quantum (only rejects\n(int)ctl->quantum < 0). With a crafted size table qdisc_pkt_len reaches\n~2 GiB, so quantum=1 makes the deficit-refill loop spin ~2^31 times\nunder the qdisc lock (a soft lockup / denial of service).\n\nAdd max(256U, ...) matching fq_codel_change(). Reject quantum > 1<<20\nwith -EINVAL, matching fq_codel_change() and the init clamp.\n\nConditions to recreate the bug:\n  CONFIG_NET_SCH_SFQ=y. Requires CAP_NET_ADMIN (namespace-local via\n  unshare -Urn suffices).\n\n  tc qdisc add dev dummy0 root sfq\n  tc qdisc change dev dummy0 root sfq quantum 1 stab data 32768 size_log 15 cell_log 0", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:12:17", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4117c528b2de5fdc3e4a7e3626815b616a635cdc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f82fa6f10d4a69322cad0f7a4aa523ce6292a5a0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0692ce5a528df450d64e9f819054177e9d91076f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e4192bcf83aaab02129644ddf4656fd86e93751f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f3820dce042a673fcb28cc31c87ee14257e21a17", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/534cd7ecbbc6e8a974f4003a5c1557439c6e0a72", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e6c1cb728e389354203a72bc77464c222a247aeb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fb9f88a33c516ea5c0bcd9a22ca288b246b34567"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98012", "GHSA-wq2r-f96j-67j9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "08a8fd19-2de2-36c2-8a27-a8441c94a8c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "1fa2d7f6-8144-3c5f-b357-134ab30beb4a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "26dbeca2-80